Based on the search results, here's what I found about Next.js 16.2 new features and the experimental `appNewScrollHandler`:

## Next.js 16.2 Overview

Next.js 16.2 is now available with highlights including ~400% faster next dev startup, ~50% faster rendering, a redesigned default error page, Turbopack improvements with 200+ bug fixes, and AI enhancements.

## Experimental appNewScrollHandler

The new handler improves how focus is managed after navigations, and instead of focusing the first focusable descendant deep within a segment (which could skip past content), it now blurs the active element, matching how browser navigations work.

To enable this experimental feature, you can configure it in your `next.config.js`:

```javascript
const nextConfig = {
